.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Represents a layered mathematical canvas system composed of multiple sub‑canvases\&. Each layer is a deterministic transformation applied on top of the base canvas, forming a purely mathematical composition model rather than a graphical drawing system\&. 

Layers do not store rendered pixels\&. Instead, each layer contributes transformation rules, blend operations, or color modifications that are applied when the final pixel buffer is requested through \fBGetPixels\fP or when swapped into another canvas via \fBSwapIn\fP\&.

.PP
The system is fully deterministic: the same layer configuration always produces the same composed result\&.

.PP
\fBTemplate Parameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIT\fP The color type used by the canvas\&.
.RE
.PP

