.SS "bool SystemEx\&.Drawing\&.ICanvasList< T >\&.SetShowing (bool show, int index)"

.PP
Sets the visibility state of the specified layer\&. A hidden layer does not participate in the mathematical composition when \fBGetPixels\fP is invoked\&. Layer index semantics: \fR0\fP refers to the base canvas, \fR1\fP refers to the first added layer, \fR2\fP to the second, and so on\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIshow\fP Whether the layer should be included in composition\&.
.br
\fIindex\fP The layer index whose visibility is being changed\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
\fRtrue\fP if the visibility was changed; otherwise \fRfalse\fP\&.
.RE
.PP

.SS "int SystemEx\&.Drawing\&.ICanvasList< T >\&.SwapIn (int x, int y, int width, int height, ref ICanvas< T > toDraw)"

.PP
Swaps the mathematically composed region of this canvas into another canvas\&. The region defined by \fIx\fP , \fIy\fP , \fIwidth\fP , and \fIheight\fP  is computed mathematically and then written into \fItoDraw\fP \&. No drawing occurs; the operation transfers computed pixel values\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIx\fP The X coordinate of the region\&.
.br
\fIy\fP The Y coordinate of the region\&.
.br
\fIwidth\fP The width of the region\&.
.br
\fIheight\fP The height of the region\&.
.br
\fItoDraw\fP The target canvas receiving the computed pixels\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The number of pixels swapped\&.
.RE
.PP

